  journal     = "bioRxivorg",
  institution = "bioRxiv",
  abstract    = "Single-cell transcriptomics offers the promise of measuring the
                 diversity of cellular phenotypes across species, diseases, and
                 other biological conditions. Recently, foundation models have
                 emerged to identify this variation, yet most methods represent
                 each cell independently, despite technical limitations that
                 reduce measurement precision at the single-cell level. Here, we
